From 7161ac1843392df110135ebd333ea0e9789c671a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark <30506876+markhuguet@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:09:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] banded FA: tiled prompt kernel; optional rel_idx so
 non-contiguous caches (wrapped SWA) stay banded

- flash_attn_ext_banded_f32_tiled: for > 8 query rows, a block of 32 query-head rows (one KV head's
  group) streams K/V tiles of 32 keys through shared memory; lane-per-key scores, f32 online softmax.
- ggml_flash_attn_ext_banded_set_rel_idx (src[7]): llama's flat q*(E+1)+dist indices replace the
  K-tail alignment (CPU and all HIP banded kernels; MMA declines). Inkling routes layers whose cache
  is not position-contiguous (wrapped SWA) to the banded kernels instead of dense softmax + gathered bias.
- test-backend-ops: 4 rel_idx cases (17/17 pass vs CPU).
gfx1151 Inkling pp512 @8K 122 -> ~178 t/s (tiled +54%, rel_idx +9-12% on top), decode @8K +2-7%.
Accuracy vs an f32 CPU reference (8K ctx, 2 chunks): mean KLD tiled+rel_idx 0.168, tiled+dense 0.163,
old+dense 0.172 (+-0.009): numerically equivalent. Off switches: GGML_CUDA_BANDED_NO_TILED=1,
LLAMA_INKLING_NO_BANDED_IDX=1.
